From 49cfbd9806f849c89747dafd370fda5d402e1238 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CheezerWheezer <172987769+CheezerWheezer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:32:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] vulkan: save compiled pipelines with
 VK_KHR_pipeline_binary and accept shader caches from other drivers

AMD's Windows driver does not keep compiled pipelines between sessions the way
NVIDIA's does, so every cached pipeline is compiled again on every boot. Save
the driver's binaries per title (vulkan_binaries.fork-v54.bin) and build from
them on later runs. Pipelines from a shared cache made with another driver
are no longer dropped: their key's driver fields are rewritten to this
device's.

RX 6750 XT, driver 26.10.1, Ocarina of Time: boot to title 513 s -> 14 s with
2.9k pipelines; all 20k pipelines of a shared pack built in ~30 s instead of
10-18 min. 0.2-0.4 ms per pipeline from binaries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 88d811c6dade2f1bc33402de373af6f62a672e2e)
